WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Initialize: the app prepares this phone as a secure endpoint.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.533
Choose the input: Quantum Keyboard or the system keyboard.

3
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:16.533
Set the primary PIN that opens the app.

4
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:28.700
Add a duress PIN that wipes data and a decoy PIN that opens a fake vault. Configuration only.

5
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:39.767
Quantum Keyboard is enabled in Android settings.

6
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:49.800
Android shows its standard warning for every third-party keyboard.

7
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:56.433
Back in the app, pick Quantum Keyboard in the system picker.

8
00:00:56.433 --> 00:01:03.500
Meanwhile the app saves the PINs and creates the identity key pair (RSA-2048) in the Android Keystore.

9
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:15.700
The app opens behind a working calculator. Type the PIN and = to enter.

10
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.700
Allow notifications for messages and calls.

11
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.733
Allow background activity so messages and calls reach you.

12
00:01:23.733 --> 00:01:31.233
Home: Tor online, ready for the first contact.
